===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fro|en}} {{m|fro|plaiz}}, from {{etyl|Late Latin|en}} {{m|la|platessa}}, from {{etyl|grc|en}} {{m|grc|πλατύς||broad}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|plās}}, {{IPA|/pleɪs/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|eɪs|lang=en}}
* {{homophones|lang=en|place}}
{{rfap|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|plaice|plaices}}

# Several similar marine [[flatfish]] of family [[Pleuronectidae]] of {{vern|right-eye flounder}}s:
## ''[[Pleuronectes platessa]]'' ([[European plaice]]), commonly found in the [[North Sea]] and [[Irish Sea]], with smooth brown skin and red or orange spots.
## {{taxlink|Hippoglossoides platessoides|species|noshow=1|ver=161010}} ({{vern|American plaice}}), of the North American [[Atlantic]].
## {{taxlink|Pleuronectes quadrituberculatus|species|noshow=1|ver=161010}} ({{vern|Alaska plaice}}), of the eastern North Pacific.
## {{taxlink|Acanthopsetta nadeshnyi|species|noshow=1|ver=161010}} ({{vern|scale-eye plaice}}), of the western North Pacific.
## {{taxlink|Liopsetta glacialis|species|noshow=1|ver=161010}} ({{vern|polar plaice}})

